-## Variation
+## Variations
+
+When the Product supports alternative versions of a usage context at the same
+time, model them as **Variations**: author each as an Experience and connect them
+with `variantOf`. Both are
+current and valid. This is useful for an A/B library where one alternative also
+provides a source workspace with a bulk-read action. A different list layout alone
+would not justify another Experience.
+
+```yaml
+# interfaces/reader-mobile/experiences/source-focused-library/experience.md
+actors: [reader]
+access: authenticated
+variantOf: reader-mobile::personal-library
+```
+
+The target is another Experience in the same Interface, with no `variantOf` of
+its own. Further alternatives point to that same anchor. The link does not make
+the anchor older, preferred, a default, or a parent. It inherits no Screens,
+Capabilities, Rules, permissions or navigation. Each alternative names its own
+content, and shared Capabilities explicitly list both availability Contexts.
+
+A Business Rule targeting both Experiences states who receives each alternative,
+what happens when no assignment exists, and any requirement to keep the selection
+stable. For example: Readers assigned Classic enter Personal library; Readers
+assigned Source-focused enter Source-focused library; unassigned Readers enter
+Personal library; selection stays fixed during a session. This is authored Rule
+prose. Lint checks references, while verification checks the actual selection
+behavior; lint cannot prove that prose conditions cover every case.
+
+Use Scenarios for a conditional outcome of one ability, such as a shipping offer
+inside the same checkout. Use visual References for color, layout or ordinary
+copy changes. Distinct destinations or available abilities across the usage
+context justify separate Experiences. Structural validation does not establish
+that independent authors will always choose the same boundary.
+
+When an alternative is removed, remove or redirect its incoming links. Keep no
+historical Experience solely to preserve a Variation link; historical changes live
+in Git. No Variation list is authored on the anchor: relationships are derived from
+`variantOf`.
+
+## Other forms of variation
 
 A Product varies along a few axes without leaving the model, and each already
 has a home.
