+#### Experience Variations
+
+Optional `variantOf` names the full qualified id of another Experience in the
+same Interface. Both resources describe current, valid alternatives of the same
+usage context, such as A/B library Experiences with different destinations and
+abilities. The target must exist, differ from the source, and have no `variantOf`
+of its own: self-links, chains and cycles are invalid. Multiple alternatives
+point to one anchor. The anchor is a resource, not a default, parent, older
+release or source of inherited content. Valid links justify Experiences even
+when their audiences and access modes coincide.
+
+```yaml
+actors: [reader]
+access: authenticated
+variantOf: reader-mobile::personal-library
+```
+
+Each Experience declares its own audience, access, navigation and content;
+Capabilities explicitly name every supported availability Context, and Scenarios
+name the places where they occur. The link inherits nothing and creates no
+availability, navigation, permission or transition. Its family and backlinks are
+derived, never authored as a second membership list.
+
+Use this relationship when Variations differ in destinations or
+available abilities across a usage context. A conditional outcome of one ability
+belongs in its Scenarios; a different drawing, color or ordinary copy belongs in
+visual References. This boundary remains an authoring test, not a determinism
+claim established by structural lint.
+
+A Business Rule targeting the alternatives states who receives each, the
+unassigned case and any selection stability requirement. It is normal Rule prose,
+not a permission grant or an executable selection expression. Lint resolves the
+link and Rule targets; verification checks selection behavior and reports missing
+evidence instead of claiming the conditions are exhaustive. A selection Rule
+neither grants nor revokes permission. Shared Rules target both alternatives or
+the containing Interface explicitly; they do not propagate through `variantOf`.
+
+There is no Experience `version` field or historical resource archive. When an
+alternative is removed, remove or redirect its incoming variant links; a surviving
+single Experience has no variant link. Independently supported interaction
+contracts may be separate Interfaces; a different address or header alone does
+not decide it. Historical changes remain in Git.
 
