@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+---
+kind: edge
+routes:
+  local: Local
+steps:
+  - text: The Developer reads an Experience row and its Variation links in the Interfaces list
+    kind: actor
+    actor: developer
+    entities:
+      - { entity: interface, effect: reads, facts: [Type] }
+      - { entity: experience, effect: reads, facts: [Container, Audience, Variation] }
+    contexts:
+      local: { place: local-report-web::resource-collection }
+  - text: The Product annotates the Experience with links to its current peers without treating them as children
+    kind: product
+    entities:
+      - { entity: experience, effect: reads, facts: [Variation] }
+    contexts:
+      local: { place: local-report-web::resource-collection }
+  - text: The Developer opens an Experience and follows a card in Variations without losing the underlying list
+    kind: actor
+    actor: developer
+    entities:
+      - { entity: experience, effect: reads, facts: [Variation] }
+    contexts:
+      local: { place: local-report-web::resource-reading::overview }
+---
+
+# Read Experience Variations
+
+## Trigger
+
+The Developer wants to find the current alternatives of an Experience and read
+each one in context.
+
+## Outcome
+
+Alternatives remain peers under their owning Interface. The list annotates each
+Experience with links to its alternatives. Overview uses the same resource cards
+as Also on, while Business Rules and Connections retain their existing roles.
+Closing a reading restores the list's filters, expansion and viewport.
+
+## Edge cases
+
+- An Experience without alternatives has no empty relation label or section.
+- Peer links never become containment children or inflate expansion counts.
+- The same peer annotation appears in Interface Delivery.
+- A Variation link does not choose a default or inherit content from another resource.
